cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "canVODpy: An Open Python Ecosystem for GNSS-Transmissometry Canopy VOD Retrievals"
abstract: >
  canVODpy aims to be the central community-driven software suite for deriving canopy
  Vegetation Optical Depth (VOD) from the signal-to-noise ratio of the same GNSS
  signal, received at the same time by one receiver below the canopy and one with an
  unobstructed view of the sky. It reads RINEX v2.11, RINEX v3.04, stripped RINEX
  v3.05, NMEA v4.00, and Septentrio binary (SBF) files; computes the satellite angles
  of every observation from final orbit and clock products or from broadcast
  ephemerides; keeps observations and VOD in versioned Icechunk stores with DataCite,
  ACDD, and STAC metadata; retrieves VOD with the zeroth-order tau-omega model; and
  assigns observations to hemispheric grids.
